extra.reason:
Implemented deterministic local GitHub review packages as derived protocol files, without adding a Delivery business object or a remote provider capability.

Delivered:
- strict review-package, pull-request-preview, and zero-write dry-run contracts;
- current approved plan-review and current publication-review reconstruction guards;
- deterministic package generation from Delivery, frozen candidate, authoritative Diff, RuntimeEvents, EvidenceRefs, CriterionResults, and DeliveryVerdict;
- separate requirements, solution, plan decision, architecture, process, candidate, verification, publication context, preview, and dry-run files;
- SHA-256/byte manifest, package identity, cross-file identity verification, and stale/tampered input rejection;
- atomic local directory publication, exact replay reuse, conflict rejection, and verified readback;
- package allowlists plus README and ADR-0023 updates.

Verification:
- focused GitHub package/publication/plan-review/diagram/service tests passed;
- corepack pnpm test passed: 164 TypeScript tests and 15 Rust tests;
- full corepack pnpm verify passed, including format, lint, typecheck, clippy, CPB boundary, build, package allowlists, native installed smoke, real installed DSH Web/CLI/signal/restart smoke, upstream checks, and clean-checkout install/test/build/package verification.

Implemented fail-closed, idempotent GitHub publication control as an operational protocol rather than a new Delivery business object.

Delivered:
- strict DSH/provider adapter contract for branch, pull request, issue comment, and commit status operations;
- stable operation keys bound to the exact review package, candidate, verdict, repository, branch, and provider identity;
- provider-free default/dry-run mode with zero remote writes;
- live mode gated by the exact resolved human publication decision and current spec/candidate/verdict/destination;
- durable append-only intent and result journal, with intent persisted before provider calls and results persisted afterward;
- lookup-first reconciliation for unknown or interrupted outcomes, replay skipping of confirmed operations, and concurrency convergence to at most one remote resource per operation key;
- rejection of credential-bearing provider inputs/results while credentials and authenticated GitHub API access remain owned by DSH/provider plugins;
- package allowlist, README, ADR, and focused failure/concurrency/recovery tests.

Verification:
- 181 TypeScript tests passed;
- 15 Rust tests passed;
- full corepack pnpm verify passed, including format, lint, typecheck, clippy, CPB boundary, builds, package checks, native installed smoke, installed DSH Web/CLI/signal/restart smoke, upstream checks, and clean-checkout install/test/build/package/upstream replay.
